Z||000000||Denise||04-07-2001||08:41 AM||||Hi list! <BR>Been a while since i've posted.  <BR>I'm having troubles on both cars.  one with T-tops the wipers won't "park"<BR>the other(daily driver) the wipers won't turn off, cruise doesn't work, and the washer doesn't work. <BR>I've been told to get the parts from advance auto. switch plate for a s-10. <BR>Does anyone have a difinitve way to test all the componants before I start buying/getting parts?<BR>thanks,<BR>Denise<P>------------------<BR>Denise,Blk 86 Fiero SE, was 4 spd now 5 spd (iszsu) jasper 2.8,BFG TA's, yada yada yada..||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-07-2001||08:41 PM||||its unusual no ones replied denise. I havent had any problems with my wipers, so dont have any knowlege to pass on to you. Sounds like the stalk switch is messed up bad. May try checking all the fuses in fuseblock, these Fieros seem to have all kinds of weird electrical gremlins. Wouldnt it be great to find the cig liter fuse blown, replace it and everything works again? Id try just exhanging the wiper motor on the other one with a used one rather than trying to rebuild it unless you want to buy a new one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||04-07-2001||08:48 PM||||A couple of my cars give me a surprise wipe on occasion for no apparent reason. My guess is it's in the stalk.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||04-07-2001||08:49 PM||||For the wipers that won't 'park'.<BR>There is a small cam inside the motor housing that is obviously bad. I get them at my local Car Quest, but am sure that other parts stores can get them as well.<BR>If you have a Haynes book, go back to the schematics and locate your circuits and then locate the wires at the plug on the steering column. Locate the proper wires and jumper them to work. If they work properly, replace the stalk. If they don't, you have other problems in the wiring.||||reg||1
